  id: Gracilis_muscle.R
  partName: Gracilis_muscle.R
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'The gracilis is a long, flat muscle located on the medial side of the thigh
    and is responsible for adducting the limb. It helps bring the limb toward the
    midline of the body and supports coordinated movement. This muscle also contributes
    to stability and balance during locomotion. '
  - It works with other muscles to control limb positioning and ensure smooth transitions
    during movement, making it important for overall coordination.
